  "text": "[LEXP.3.1] `abs`, `round`, `min` and `max` are callable in any expression, with\nno declaration and no import. `floor`, `ceil`, `trunc`, `sign`, `sqrt`, `pow`, the\nangle conversions ([LEXP.3.6]) and the transcendental functions ([LEXP.3.9]) are\nmembers of the `math` module, reached through its import ([LIMP.3.3.4]). Names and\nsemantics are Python's `math` module's where the two overlap. Type signatures\nfollow [LEXP.7].\n\n",
